@startuml
title Activity Diagram - Training and evaluation (main.py train / evaluate)

|features.py|
start
:Load CSV tables\n(data_loader.py);
:Keep top-5 league matches\nand add the season from games;
:Aggregate per player and season\n(minutes, matches, goals, assists, cards,\nmain league and club);
if (minutes >= 450?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Drop row;
  stop
endif
:Join end-of-season valuation\n(latest between April and July);
:Join player profile\n(birth date, position);
if (valuation, birth date and\nposition available?) then (yes)
else (no)
  :Drop row;
  stop
endif
:Add club points per game\nand European cup minutes;
:Compute age, per-90 stats\nand log10(value);

|models.py|
:Split by season\ntrain 2012-2023 / validation 2024 / test 2025;
:Try 18 Random Forest settings:\nfit on train, MAE on validation;
:Refit best setting on 2012-2024;
|predictor.py|
:Save models/model.joblib;
note right: end of\n**main.py train**

|evaluation.py|
:Fit baselines and linear regression\non 2012-2024;
:Measure all 4 models once\non the test season 2025;
:Write metrics, plots and\nlargest gaps to reports/;
note right: **main.py evaluate**
stop
@enduml
